{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>נגששה.</b> Like נמשש, and it has no [phonetic] fault [i.e., the nun assimilation is regular]. And some say it is from the root of וגוש עפר (Job 7:5)." "<b>בצהרים.</b> Which is midday, as though we were at twilight, and this is by way of metaphor." "<b>באשמנים.</b> Some say graves. And it is possible that it is like צהרים, or like בחיים, the meaning being 'amidst the living.' And it is possible that the alef is added and the meaning is 'amidst the שמנים,' and they are the nations."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 59, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:18.187575457Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}